ueue fails or times out the event is dropped and counted in a metric, so raiser success and latency are never affected. Unhandled exception or memory leak in vendor-call code crashes only the worker process, not the app; retry with backoff then dead-letter, bounded batch and payload caps. Alerts: queue depth, send error rate, worker restarts. Volume is an unmeasured ASSUMPTION (peak under about 50 events/sec); week-1 task counts eligible events per subsystem and peak rate, higher figure triggers revisiting a full standalone split with its own datastore. 6. Timeline: this quarter ships versioned contract, worker, email and push for the highest-value subsystems with opt-in, kill-switches and 3 alerts; SMS (third channel) and remaining subsystems follow after volume is measured, so only 2 of 3 channels ship this quarter. 7. Terms: service = in-code module behind a versioned interface, run as a separately released worker process, not a networked node with own datastore; deployment = worker image rollout, about 10 min, not the 45 min whole-monolith release; outage = unhandled exception or memory leak in the worker process (contained to it) or queue backlog; whole-app outage from this code is removed from the request path. Judged on what it does, not the words.]]>
